      ":question/worked-solution": "The order of an ordinary differential equation (ODE) is the order of the highest derivative in the equation.\n\nThe highest derivative in the given ODE is $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{5}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{5}},$ which has order $5.$\n\nTherefore, the order of the ODE is $5.$",
